  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Find the values of $x$ for which:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q1a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x(x-1)(x+1)>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1<x<0$ or $x>1$.",
          "worked": "The zeroes are $-1,0,1$. Each is simple, so the graph crosses the axis at each zero. The leading coefficient is positive.\n\nThe graph is above the axis on $(-1,0)$ and $(1,\\infty)$. Hence $-1<x<0$ or $x>1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x-2)(x+2)(x+3)\\le0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-3$ or $-2\\le x\\le2$.",
          "worked": "The zeroes are $-3,-2,2$. Each is simple, and the leading coefficient is positive.\n\nThe graph is below the axis for $x<-3$ and $-2<x<2$. Include the zeroes because equality is allowed: $x\\le-3$ or $-2\\le x\\le2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$-x(x-2)(x+4)\\ge0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-4$ or $0\\le x\\le2$.",
          "worked": "The zeroes are $-4,0,2$. Each is simple, and the leading coefficient is negative.\n\nThe graph is above the axis for $x<-4$ and $0<x<2$. Including the zeroes gives $x\\le-4$ or $0\\le x\\le2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(2x+3)(4x+5)(6x+7)<0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-\\frac32$ or $-\\frac54<x<-\\frac76$.",
          "worked": "The zeroes, in increasing order, are $-\\frac32,-\\frac54,-\\frac76$. Each is simple, and the leading coefficient is positive.\n\nThe graph is below the axis for $x<-\\frac32$ and $-\\frac54<x<-\\frac76$. The strict inequality excludes all three zeroes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
